      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a triangle given its vertices \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\), we can use the Shoelace (or GC) theorem. This theorem states that for a triangle with vertices \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\), the area \\(A\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1y_2 + x_2y_3 + x_3y_1 - (y_1x_2 + y_2x_3 + y_3x_1) \\right|\n\\]\n\nGiven vertices:\n- \\((x_1, y_1) = (0,0)\\)\n- \\((x_2, y_2) = (0,5)\\)\n- \\((x_3, y_3) = (7,12)\\)\n\nLet's plug these values into the Shoelace formula and calculate the area.\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 \\cdot 5 + 0 \\cdot 12 + 7 \\cdot 0 - (0 \\cdot 0 + 5 \\cdot 7 + 12 \\cdot 0) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSimplifying inside the absolute value expression:\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + 0 + 0 - (0 + 35 + 0) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 - 35 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 35 = 17.5\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is \\(17.5\\) square units.\n\nLet's verify this calculation using Python.\n```python\n# Define the vertices of the triangle\nx1, y1 = 0, 0\nx2, y2 = 0, 5\nx3, y3 = 7, 12\n\n# Compute the area using the Shoelace formula\narea = 0.5 * abs(x1*y2 + x2*y3 + x3*y1 - (y1*x2 + y2*x3 + y3*x1))\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n17.5\n```\nThe area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\) is \\(\\boxed{17.5}\\) square units.",
